+**CORRECTION (2026-09-23).** This section audited the style-mask *constants* but missed
+the *setter*: `-[NSWindow setStyleMask:]` is **10.6+**. Before 10.6 a window's style mask is
+fixed at creation and the selector does not exist at all, so every call raises
+`NSInvalidArgumentException` (`*** -[MpvVideoWindow setStyleMask:]: unrecognized selector`,
+reported on 10.5; 10.6 is unaffected). The row above calling the borderless manual-fullscreen
+branch "already 10.5-safe" is therefore wrong, as is the `setStyleMask:NSBorderlessWindowMask`
+recipe in `COCOA-PORT-PLAN.md` §4. Affected call sites were `window.m` `-setFullScreen:`
+(enter/exit) and `-updateBorder:` (runtime `--border` toggling).
+
+Fixed by making `-setStyleMask:` a no-op below 10.6 (probed with
+`[NSWindow instancesRespondToSelector:]`, since the subclass overrides the selector and would
+always answer YES to `-respondsToSelector:`) and adding `-setLegacyFullScreen:onScreen:`: a
+second, borderless `MpvVideoWindow` covers the screen and the view hierarchy — and with it the
+`NSOpenGLContext` drawable — is moved across by
+`-[MpvCocoaAdapter moveContentViewToWindow:]`. Runtime border toggling remains impossible on
+10.5 (the mask picked by `create_window()` at startup is final); `--border=no` at startup
+still works. 10.6+ keeps the in-place `setStyleMask:` path, with the probe compiled out to a
+constant `YES`.
+
 **Net recommendation:** Strip out the entire Lion `NSWindowDelegate` fullscreen protocol
 conformance and the `toggleFullScreen:` override. Keep only the pre-existing "else" /
 non-native manual fullscreen logic (borderless window + `setFrame:` to screen frame,
